diff --git a/.changeset/normative-dwi.md b/.changeset/normative-dwi.md
new file mode 100644
index 00000000..29ec3c19
--- /dev/null
+++ b/.changeset/normative-dwi.md
@@ -0,0 +1,5 @@
+---
+"normative-dwi": minor
+---
+
+New app: Normative DWI scores one person's DTI and NODDI maps (FA, MD, ICVF, ISOVF, OD) against voxelwise normative models of the UK Biobank population and writes a z-score map for each, entirely in the browser. It reads PCNtoolkit warped Bayesian linear regression models from an nmzarr (Zarr v3) model store chosen by URL or local folder, checks that each map sits on the UK Biobank 2 mm template grid, and scores with a float64 CPU kernel that reproduces PCNtoolkit to better than 1e-6, or with WebGPU in float32 (within 1e-3, falling back to the CPU). Outputs are NIfTI z-score images on the input grid.
diff --git a/docs/architecture/offline-executables.md b/docs/architecture/offline-executables.md
index 10b8c5c4..c1ce9fcf 100644
--- a/docs/architecture/offline-executables.md
+++ b/docs/architecture/offline-executables.md
@@ -63,6 +63,7 @@ Paths in this table are relative to the repository root. Existing implementation
 | `nesvor` | Slice-to-volume MRI reconstruction | `exes/compute-server` runs the pinned CUDA container on Linux with NVIDIA. Its archive includes the browser frontend; Docker, model preparation and real CUDA validation remain separate. |
 | `dicom2vid` | Volume-to-video conversion | `packages/dicom2vid/bin/dicom2vid.js` runs the app's readers, series selection and frame pipeline from `packages/dicom2vid`, draws frames into buffers and encodes VP9 with libvpx (libav.js WebAssembly) into the app's muxers; `exes/node-cli` packages it for Linux x64, Windows x64 and macOS arm64. Its release check holds frame count, size, timing and key frames to the recorded Chromium videos. WebM frame PSNR compares with both recorded browser frames and rendered source; MP4 frame PSNR compares with rendered source. Windowing, rotation and stretching remain web-only; MP4 is VP9, not H.264. |
 | `surfannotate` | No default batch equivalent | Manual surface ROI drawing and vertex selection. Excluded from this rollout. |
+| `normative-dwi` | Voxelwise normative z-maps for DTI/NODDI maps | No public batch equivalent yet (PCNtoolkit predict on the same models gives the same z-scores). A Node command line around the app's own `model-store`, `predictor` and `subject-image` modules is straightforward once a public model store exists. |
 | `zarro` | No default batch equivalent | Interactive OME-Zarr exploration. Conversion or extraction would be a separately scoped command. |
 | `dicomview` | No default batch equivalent | Interactive DICOM browsing. Its batch steps already ship as command lines: dcm2niix for conversion and dicompare for protocol summaries and checks. |
 
